􀢄  Test run with 37 tests in 6 suites failed after 64.075 seconds with 1 issue.
Note: Some test targets reported failures:
  - MultiModalKitTests (Swift Testing)

WHY (found after): the row lands both files, truncates model.bin, and calls ensure() again at once.
The first task's didFinishDownloadingTo had been processed (the waiters answered) but its
didCompleteWithError had not yet arrived — so getAllTasks() still listed it, state != .completed,
and the second transfer ADOPTED it as model.bin's task. Its completion then cleared the file's task
with no landing ever to follow: the transfer waited for its full minute. Fixed in ModelDownloader:
every relay event names its task; the actor keeps the identifiers of tasks whose landing it has
processed, never adopts one of those, and hears only a file's CURRENT task. 14 loop runs green after
(one run took 16 s: the background session's daemon stalled two rows at once, then delivered —
a daemon pause, not a test's wait; both rows passed).
